prompt:
Implement Sokoban in 3D using Three.js: an 8×8 grid, three boxes, three targets, a player sphere, undo, and reset.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules inside <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Level]
(1) Use an 8×8 grid; generate a solvable level randomly or with a fixed seed, containing 3 boxes, 3 targets, walls, and empty spaces;
(2) Use a ground plane, represent walls as cubes, and distinguish target cells using color/markers;

[Player]
(3) Represent the player as a colored SphereGeometry occupying one cell;
(4) Each valid WASD input moves one cell at a time (mapped to row/col);

[Pushing]
(5) If the next cell in the movement direction contains a box and the cell behind that box is empty, move both the player and the box forward by one cell;
(6) If the cell behind the box contains a wall or another box, do not move; boxes cannot be pushed beyond the boundary;
(7) Increment moves by 1 after each valid move;

[Victory]
(8) When all three boxes are on targets, set levelComplete=true;

[Buttons]
(9) id="undoBtn": undo one move, restoring positions and moves;
(10) id="resetBtn": reset the level with moves=0 and levelComplete=false;

[State Exposure (Required)]
(11) After every move, expose window.__3D_STATE__:
  - playerPos:{row,col} 0..7
  - boxes:[{row,col}]×3
  - targets:[{row,col}]×3
  - moves, boxesOnTarget 0..3, levelComplete

[Evaluation Helper (Recommended)]
(12) window.__STATEPROBE_move__('W'|'A'|'S'|'D') must behave consistently with keyboard input.

Output a single HTML file that runs when opened directly in a browser.
